  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "37130510",
      "title": "Working with \"Configuration Objects\" (Non-Widget Objects)",
      "lectureOrder": 30,
      "videoOrder": 27,
      "sourceHash": "79a324be5683ef0ddadca317339eda4d1a61c1970cbf87a92a3762a65bad109b",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.07,
          "end": 5.34,
          "en": "So knowing about this objects concept",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.34,
          "end": 8.46,
          "en": "is crucial because all values are objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.46,
          "end": 9.99,
          "en": "in the end as you learned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.99,
          "end": 12.27,
          "en": "But here, my goal is not to set this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.27,
          "end": 14.85,
          "en": "just to some purple background color.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.85,
          "end": 17.253,
          "en": "Instead, I want it to have a nice gradient.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.42,
          "end": 21.03,
          "en": "Now this can't be achieved with backgroundColor",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.03,
          "end": 23.67,
          "en": "because that wants a single color.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.67,
          "end": 27.92,
          "en": "And Scaffold also has no other argument that we could set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.92,
          "end": 32.01,
          "en": "that would allow us to add a gradient background.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.01,
          "end": 35.88,
          "en": "Instead, what we can do here is we can add another new",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.88,
          "end": 40.65,
          "en": "widget between Scaffold and Center so that it wraps Center",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.65,
          "end": 43.17,
          "en": "and therefore implicitly also text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.17,
          "end": 46.143,
          "en": "by right-clicking on Center and refactoring this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.98,
          "end": 50.04,
          "en": "And here we wanna wrap this with a container,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 50.04,
          "end": 52.5,
          "en": "which is another widget provided by Flutter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.5,
          "end": 55.379,
          "en": "and Container is a widget that's very useful",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.379,
          "end": 59.52,
          "en": "for configuring styling and layout settings.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 59.52,
          "end": 61.23,
          "en": "Now here, after adding Container,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.23,
          "end": 64.38,
          "en": "I get some red squiggly lines, and if we hover over that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 64.38,
          "end": 67.2,
          "en": "we learn that we should remove const",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 67.2,
          "end": 69.21000000000001,
          "en": "because that seems to be responsible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.21000000000001,
          "end": 70.953,
          "en": "for these red squiggly lines.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 71.85,
          "end": 74.13,
          "en": "And indeed, if you remove const here in front",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.13,
          "end": 78,
          "en": "of MaterialApp, they go away and you can now re-add const",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 78,
          "end": 79.35,
          "en": "in front of Center.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.35,
          "end": 81.36,
          "en": "Container is simply a widget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 81.36,
          "end": 84.24,
          "en": "provided by Flutter that doesn't support",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 84.24,
          "end": 85.588,
          "en": "setting it to const,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 85.588,
          "end": 88.96000000000001,
          "en": "and therefore you also can't set some parent widget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 88.96000000000001,
          "end": 92.78999999999999,
          "en": "that's higher up in this widget tree to const.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 92.78999999999999,
          "end": 95.34,
          "en": "It is what it is, but your IDE clearly tells you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 95.34,
          "end": 99.12299999999999,
          "en": "where you can and can't add const, so that's pretty good.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 100.53,
          "end": 103.28999999999999,
          "en": "But of course we got more blue squiggly lines here now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 103.28999999999999,
          "end": 106.38,
          "en": "But the reason for that simply is that at the moment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 106.38,
          "end": 108.63,
          "en": "dart and our code editor thinks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 108.63,
          "end": 112.83,
          "en": "that we're unnecessarily using Container, and we do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 112.83,
          "end": 115.68,
          "en": "If we don't configure anything, it's a useless wrapper",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 115.68,
          "end": 117.63,
          "en": "because if you save this and you reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 117.63,
          "end": 120.12,
          "en": "you will see that nothing changes about the app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 120.12,
          "end": 121.65,
          "en": "except for the background color.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 121.65,
          "end": 124.56,
          "en": "Since I removed the background color on Scaffold,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 124.56,
          "end": 126.78,
          "en": "but nothing else changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 126.78,
          "end": 130.14,
          "en": "But of course, our plan is not to do nothing here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 130.14,
          "end": 133.77,
          "en": "Instead, Container now also gives you many useful arguments",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 133.77,
          "end": 135.24,
          "en": "that you can set.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 135.24,
          "end": 139.36,
          "en": "For example, it provides a decoration argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 139.36,
          "end": 142.98,
          "en": "and this allows you to add various kinds of,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 142.98,
          "end": 145.65,
          "en": "well, decoration to the container",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 145.65,
          "end": 148.07999999999998,
          "en": "and therefore also to the child elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 148.07999999999998,
          "end": 149.373,
          "en": "inside of that container.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 150.78,
          "end": 154.53,
          "en": "Now, Decoration wants a decoration argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 154.53,
          "end": 156.93,
          "en": "so a argument of type Decoration,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 156.93,
          "end": 160.11,
          "en": "and such a value can be created, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 160.11,
          "end": 164.1,
          "en": "with the built-in BoxDecoration constructor function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 164.1,
          "end": 168,
          "en": "There actually also is a decoration option here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 168,
          "end": 169.619,
          "en": "in this suggestions menu,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 169.619,
          "end": 172.62,
          "en": "but this is actually not the right thing to use here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 172.62,
          "end": 175.35,
          "en": "Indeed, you can't use it if you try to use it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 175.35,
          "end": 177.54,
          "en": "because it's a so-called abstract class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 177.54,
          "end": 179.67000000000002,
          "en": "And we'll learn more about classes later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 179.67000000000002,
          "end": 182.28,
          "en": "For the moment, it's enough to know that you can't use that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 182.28,
          "end": 186.24,
          "en": "but you can use this BoxDecoration constructor function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 186.24,
          "end": 190.23,
          "en": "and this will then also give you such a decoration object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 190.23,
          "end": 192.9,
          "en": "Of course, it will give you a BoxDecoration object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 192.9,
          "end": 196.02,
          "en": "but as you learned, the values can be of multiple types",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 196.02,
          "end": 200.67000000000002,
          "en": "and BoxDecoration objects are also of type decoration.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 200.67000000000002,
          "end": 204.12,
          "en": "Just as MaterialApp is not just of type MaterialApp,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 204.12,
          "end": 206.34,
          "en": "but also of type widget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 206.34,
          "end": 207.99,
          "en": "This might all sound confusing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 207.99,
          "end": 209.46,
          "en": "but you're just learning it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 209.46,
          "end": 211.11,
          "en": "You're just getting started with it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 211.11,
          "end": 214.02,
          "en": "You will get a lot of experience with that over time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 214.02,
          "end": 216.03300000000002,
          "en": "as you're using all these features.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 217.41,
          "end": 220.95,
          "en": "Now, this BoxDecoration constructor function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 220.95,
          "end": 222.12,
          "en": "which we're calling here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 222.12,
          "end": 224.73,
          "en": "to build such a BoxDecoration object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 224.73,
          "end": 229.41,
          "en": "then also supports various arguments that can be set.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 229.41,
          "end": 231.78,
          "en": "For example, the gradient argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 231.78,
          "end": 235.05,
          "en": "which sounds just about right for what we're planning to do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 235.05,
          "end": 237.723,
          "en": "because our goal is to add a gradient here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 239.67000000000002,
          "end": 242.07,
          "en": "So the gradient argument can be set here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 242.07,
          "end": 246.15,
          "en": "and that then wants a value of type gradient.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 246.15,
          "end": 248.76,
          "en": "Now, there are different ways of creating gradients.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 248.76,
          "end": 250.86,
          "en": "For example, a RadialGradient",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 250.86,
          "end": 253.863,
          "en": "or what I wanna do here, a LinearGradient.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 254.85,
          "end": 256.62,
          "en": "This is another constructor function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 256.62,
          "end": 258.48,
          "en": "that creates a LinearGradient,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 258.48,
          "end": 260.31,
          "en": "which is also of type gradient",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 260.31,
          "end": 261.99,
          "en": "and which therefore is a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 261.99,
          "end": 264.9,
          "en": "we can set for this gradient argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 264.9,
          "end": 268.11,
          "en": "And this LinearGradient constructor function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 268.11,
          "end": 270.27,
          "en": "wants even more arguments.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 270.27,
          "end": 272.58,
          "en": "And what we're doing here is quite typical",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 272.58,
          "end": 274.2,
          "en": "for Flutter development.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 274.2,
          "end": 276.99,
          "en": "You often end up nesting widgets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 276.99,
          "end": 280.44,
          "en": "and/or configuration objects into each other",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 280.44,
          "end": 282.57,
          "en": "so that they can work together",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 282.57,
          "end": 285.603,
          "en": "and give you the overall desired user interface.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 286.62,
          "end": 288.57,
          "en": "Don't forget to add those commas",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 288.57,
          "end": 291.21,
          "en": "after all the closing parentheses to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 291.21,
          "end": 293.58,
          "en": "that your code is styled in a readable way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 293.58,
          "end": 295.2,
          "en": "so that you never lose track",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 295.2,
          "end": 297.99,
          "en": "of how these things are related.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 297.99,
          "end": 300.69,
          "en": "And here for a LinearGradient, there are again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 300.69,
          "end": 302.25,
          "en": "more things we can set.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 302.25,
          "end": 305.28,
          "en": "Most importantly, this colors thing here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 305.28,
          "end": 306.843,
          "en": "this colors argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 307.68,
          "end": 312.123,
          "en": "And this colors argument now wants a special kind of value.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
